cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cross-scale organisation of the atmospheric circulation: a falsification-grade research programme (Shroedinger, gen4)"
version: "6.0"
type: software
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/Shroedinger"
url: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/Shroedinger"
date-released: 2026-08-19
authors:
  - family-names: "Sotiriadi"
    given-names: "N."
abstract: >-
  Preregistered research programme on the cross-scale organisation of the
  atmospheric circulation. The surviving invariant is P: the
  surrogate-anchored coupling between the spatial envelopes of adjacent
  scale bands of the 850 hPa relative vorticity field. P is a season-,
  year- and ENSO-stable regional signature, replicated in an independent
  reanalysis and in a free-running CMIP6 HighResMIP integration that
  assimilates no atmospheric observations, mapped globally over 936 tiles
  and attributed to convective regime and storm-track activity, while
  having no accessible dynamics of its own. A theory candidate
  (quenched-texture organisation) carries five scored predictions, four
  supported and one failed. Four methods audits establish that the
  estimator is neither the amplitude-modulation coefficient of wall
  turbulence nor a cascade/intermittency statistic, that its rank
  construction is decoration, and that the map's reliability ceiling is
  R^2 = 0.914 rather than the cross-season 0.603 used earlier - so the
  attribution explains 59 per cent of the reproducible variance and the
  remainder is a reproducible, non-spectral field whose drivers are named
  as future work. The repository contains all frozen protocols with
  deviation logs, the reconciliation scoreboard, numerical results and the
  complete catalogue of negative results.
keywords:
  - hierarchical organisation of geosystems
  - invariants
  - scale
  - atmospheric dynamics
  - ERA5
  - MERRA-2
  - regionalisation
  - downscaling
  - preregistration
  - negative results
